  "notes": "Chain over activities (computation execution or one hop); critical wait = s - earliest start of the blocked activity; check2 = rows tile [0, a]. Defer: blocked.can + blocked.dur + blocker.dur (on the contended resource) <= D(b). Reroute window = [r(b), r(b) + f(b) - s(b)] with s(b) the backend start_time (last-hop issue), b's own records excluded; path search is BFS on directed links minus the contended one. Round 2: PRIMARY categories are *_local (pairwise defer + local reroute = remainder of b's branch from the contended link's upstream node, idle over b's hold window); the whole-path categories are kept as secondary. Reorder: per resource, durations and the order on all other resources fixed; release = current earliest start; tail = longest path from the item's finish to the end without that resource's order edges; gain = current max(f+q) - max(Schrage EDF, longest path avoiding the resource); gain_ub uses the preemptive Jackson / busy_end+min tail lower bounds. Per-resource gains are not additive; the headline is the best single resource. BusyBarn routing is already congestion-aware static Dijkstra (gamma=100), so reroute measures runtime rerouting on top of it."
